  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"0.2.2\"\n\npackage:\n  name: dftbephy\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/CoMeT4MatSci/dftbephy/archive/refs/tags/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 338502076e91f7347787e847c25598a1dd7da90af1d0a5d0665e186e072dd109\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  skip: match(python, \"<3.10\") or match(python, \">=3.13\") or win\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ stdlib(\"c\") }}\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('cxx') }}\n  host:\n    - python\n    - pip\n    - wheel\n    - setuptools\n    - cython\n    - numpy\n  run:\n    - python\n    - numpy\n    - scipy\n    - phonopy >=3.0.0,<=3.5.1\n    - spglib <2.7\n    - h5py\n    - hsd-python\n    - mpi4py\n    - openmpi\n\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - dftbephy\n        - dftbephy.extensions\n      pip_check: false\n  - script:\n      - dftbephy --help\n\nabout:\n  license: MIT\n  license_file: LICENSE.txt\n  summary: Calculating electron-phonon couplings with DFTB\n  description: |\n    DFTBephy is a Python package for calculating electron-phonon\n    couplings based on the density-functional tight-binding (DFTB)\n    method. It also supports the calculations of electronic and phonon\n    band structures, electron-phonon scattering rates, and electronic\n    conductivity.\n\n    Reference:\n\n    Croy, A., Unsal, E., Biele, R., and Pecchia, A.\n    Journal of Computational Electronics 22, 1231 (2023).\n    DOI: 10.1007/s10825-023-02033-9\n\n\n  homepage: https://github.com/CoMeT4MatSci/dftbephy\n  repository: https://github.com/CoMeT4MatSci/dftbephy\n  documentation: https://comet4matsci.github.io/dftbephy/main/about.html\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - acroy\n    - efunsal\n",
